 COMBINED SYNOPSIS/SOLICITATION:  

This is a combined synopsis/solicitation for commercial services prepared in accordance with FAR Part 12.&nbsp; This announcement constitutes the only solicitation; quotations are being requested, and a separate written solicitation will not be attached.&nbsp; This requirement utilizes North American Industry Classification System Code (NAICS) is 811310, with a size standard of $12.5 Million. Solicitation W50S9H27QA991 incorporates provisions and clauses by reference. The full text of provisions and clauses may be accessed electronically at www.acquisition.gov. 



 DESCRIPTION OF REQUIREMENT:  5 Year Blanket Purchase Agreement (BPA) for Portable Fire Extinguisher Inspection, Maintenance, Recharge, Repair, and Hydrostatic Testing Services 



The Contractor shall provide all management, labor, supervision, tools, materials, equipment, transportation, replacement parts, consumable extinguishing agents, quality control, and incidental services necessary to perform portable fire extinguisher pickup, transportation, inspection, maintenance, recharge, internal examination, hydrostatic testing, repair, documentation, and return services, as required by individual Blanket Purchase Agreement (BPA) calls. 



Reference attached Statement of Work (SOW) for detailed information.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 



The anticipated Period of Performance (POP) is 15 December 2026 &ndash; 14 December 2031. 



 EVALUATION OF OFFERS:  

The Government will award a single Blanket Purchase Agreement (BPA) resulting from this solicitation to the offer responsible, whose offer conforms to the solicitation.&nbsp; The Government will evaluate offers based on price. 



Price - All offers will be evaluated according to the vendors prices submitted to the Government in accordance with the Statement of Work. 



The Government intends to evaluate offers and award a single blanket purchase agreement without discussions.&nbsp; Therefore, the Offeror&#39;s initial offer should contain the Offeror&#39;s best terms from a price standpoint.    



